# Normalize line endings to LF for all text — prevents CRLF drift on Windows
# from breaking the cross-platform gate (tests, prettier, lint).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binaries (none yet, but future-proofed)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db binary

# Lockfile: text but not diffed inline (large, machine-generated)
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated=true

# Fleet-collision absorber: every lane's flight-end regenerates this doc's
# DATA:SUMMARY block and appends a dated §8 evidence entry, so N concurrent
# lanes = N divergent edits to the same file — the single most recurrent
# sync-back conflict in flight history. `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides'
# lines: appends (the §8 log) merge losslessly, and the regenerated summary
# block is self-healing — the next flight-end `generate-data.mjs` run
# rewrites it wholesale from store data, so brief line duplication there
# never survives a flight.
docs/SELF-STUDY/PAPER.md merge=union

# Same absorber for the epic docs (EVALUATION 2026-09-03 sync-conflict
# taxonomy): the dominant remaining strand class is two same-round lanes each
# APPENDING an evolution/freshness paragraph to the same epic doc — parallel
# insertions at the same anchor, which three-way merge cannot order. Union
# keeps both paragraphs; prose dedup (two tellings of one change) is exactly
# the KEEPER page-upkeep duty and self-heals next round, same trade PAPER.md
# already made. Code files stay OUT of union on purpose: interleaved code is
# not self-healing — that class escalates to rerere or the resolution agent.
docs/epics/*.md merge=union
